### Security Concerns

#### 1. ⚠️ Secrets Hardcoded in Version Control
The `.env.test` file contains credentials that appear in the repository. Even if these are "canary" test values, having this file committed is dangerous because:

```bash
# These patterns will expose secrets in git history
